          "title": "You'll want to know: सन्तुष्टः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सन्तुष्टः — santuṣṭaḥ — \"satisfied; contented\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "यदि परिणामः शुभः अस्ति, तर्हि पिता सन्तुष्टः भवति। yadi pariṇāmaḥ śubhaḥ asti, tarhi pitā santuṣṭaḥ bhavati. If the result is good, father is satisfied."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सन्तुष्टः (santuṣṭaḥ) is built on sam, \"fully\", and tuṣṭa, \"pleased\", the past participle of the root √tuṣ, \"to be pleased\", which also gives tuṣyati; MW gives saṃtuṣṭa as quite satisfied, contented, well pleased (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
